From 587bec52029c73d8f9a5fd8ce1663939d7991639 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zibran Khan <kali834x@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:09:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fontselect: fix double free of embedded font data on add
 failure

ass_font_provider_add_font releases the font's private data via
the provider's destroy_font callback on every error path. For
embedded fonts that is destroy_font_ft, which already closes the
face and frees the FontDataFT, so the extra free(ft) in
process_fontdata freed it a second time whenever adding the font
failed (e.g. on allocation failure).

Upstream: https://github.com/libass/libass/commit/587bec52029c73d8f9a5fd8ce1663939d7991639
---
 libass/ass_fontselect.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libass/ass_fontselect.c b/libass/ass_fontselect.c
index 2303876..6038d3d 100644
--- a/libass/ass_fontselect.c
+++ b/libass/ass_fontselect.c
@@ -1000,7 +1000,6 @@ static void process_fontdata(ASS_FontProvider *priv, int idx)
         if (!ass_font_provider_add_font(priv, &info, NULL, face_index, ft)) {
             ass_msg(library, MSGL_WARN, "Failed to add embedded font '%s'",
                     name);
-            free(ft);
         }
 
         free_font_info(&info);
